# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Tags: TA tags every window and door of the storey outside its wall, TG tags
# the element clicked. A tag shows its element's type and follows it: a
# window given another type shows the new name, a window deleted loses its
# tag. Tags survive .bim and .ifcx.
import examples/bim-slice/bim_editor.dl

function list tag test tags of {bim model record:modelValue} labelled {a string:title}:
    execute:
        print ((title + (the string form of " ")) + (the string form of (the length of (modelValue's tags's values)))) as a line
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of (modelValue's tags's values):
            set tagValue to the item at cursor in (modelValue's tags's values)
            set target to the bim tag anchor of tagValue's elementId in modelValue
            set away to the cad distance from target's origin to tagValue's place
            print ((the string form of "  ") + ((the bim tag text of tagValue's elementId in modelValue) + ((the string form of ", ") + ((the bim millimetre text of away) + (the string form of " mm from it"))))) as a line

set editor to a new bim editor
set e to the address of editor
add bim example building to e
refresh bim editor e
type bim editor key 2031 in e
print editor's message as a line
list tag test tags of editor's documentValue's current labelled (the string form of "after TA:")
# A tag on a wall by a click on it.
set firstWall to the item at 0 in (editor's documentValue's current's walls's values)
set onWall to a cad vector2 with x ((firstWall's start's x + firstWall's finish's x) * 0.5) and y ((firstWall's start's y + firstWall's finish's y) * 0.5)
type bim editor key 2030 in e
move bim editor pointer to onWall within 0.1 in e
press bim editor pointer in e
release bim editor pointer in e
print editor's message as a line
# The first window takes another type; the second window goes.
set modelNow to editor's documentValue's current
set firstOpening to the item at 0 in (modelNow's openings's values)
begin bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
set otherType to add bim opening type named (the string form of "small") sized 0.6 by 0.6 with sill 1.2 and frame 0.05 to (the address of (editor's documentValue's current))
commit bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
begin bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
ignore set bim opening firstOpening's id type to otherType in (the address of (editor's documentValue's current))
ignore delete bim opening (the item at 1 in (editor's documentValue's current's openings's values))'s id from (the address of (editor's documentValue's current))
commit bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
set reread to the bim model parsed from (the bim file text of editor's documentValue's current)
print ((the string form of ".bim read: ") + (the string form of reread's valid)) as a line
list tag test tags of reread's modelValue labelled (the string form of "from .bim:")
set native to the bim native text of ifcx (the bim ifcx text of editor's documentValue's current identified as (the string form of "t.ifcx") for project (the string form of "t") by (the string form of "test") at (the string form of "2026-10-09T00:00:00Z"))
set fromIfcx to the bim model parsed from native's text
print ((the string form of ".ifcx read: ") + (the string form of fromIfcx's valid)) as a line
list tag test tags of fromIfcx's modelValue labelled (the string form of "from .ifcx:")
